ool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.01641552743613911,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":33.6,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":1.1813951978645,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.57864,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"BioNTech SE, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the development and commercialization of immunotherapies in Germany. The company offers BNT162, an mRNA vaccine for the treatment of SARS-CoV-2 virus. It also develops oncology drugs under Phase III clinical trial, including Gotistobart for metastatic non-small cell lung cancer, Pumitamig for small cell lung cancer and advanced/metastatic triple-negative breast cancer, and Trastuzumab pamirtecan for metastatic breast cancer and epirubicin and cyclophosphamide; and drugs under Phase 2/3 clinical trial, such as BNT113 for human papillomavirus and head and neck squamous cell carcinoma, as well as Pumitamig for metastatic colorectal and non-small cell lung cancer. In addition, the company engages in the development of oncology drugs under Phase II clinical trial comprising BNT116 for advance non-small cell lung cancer, BNT326/YL202 for multiple solid tumors and advanced/metastatic breast cancer, Autogene cevumeran for advance colorectal cancer, and Gotistobart for platinum-resistant ovarian cancer, as well as Pumitamig for glioblastoma, hepatocellular carcinoma, malignant pleural mesothelioma, neuroendocrine neoplasms, and metastatic pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma. Further, it develops BNT166 which is Phase II clinical trial for mpox virus; and infectious diseases drugs under Phase 1/2 clinical trial, which include BNT162 + BNT161 for SARS-CoV-2 and influenza, BNT164 for tuberculosis, BNT165 for malaria, and BNT166 for mpox. The company was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in Mainz, Germany.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Ugur  Sahin M.D. | Co-Founder, CEO & Chair of the Management Board | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $405K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 73%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $40K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["BioNTech SE is a large-cap healthcare business with a $21.2B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -44% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +19.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 84% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $310M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -20.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 58% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 49% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $84.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 28% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 149% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Healthcare peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How New Patent Lawsuits Will Impact BioNTech (BNTX) Investors","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-bntx/biontech/news/how-new-patent-lawsuits-will-impact-biontech-bntx-investors","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794583516.987,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"BioNTech (BNTX) Is Facing Fresh Global Patent Lawsuits","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-bntx/biontech/news/biontech-bntx-is-facing-fresh-global-patent-lawsuits","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794396204.584,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"BioNTech (NASDAQ: BNTX) agrees to buy FDA priority review voucher for $205 million","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/biontech-nasdaq-bntx-agrees-to-buy-fda-priority-review-voucher-for-205-million.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794338144.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","regulatory"]},{"title":"BioNTech (BNTX) Stock Looks Above Fair Value On Current Sales","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-bntx/biontech/news/biontech-bntx-stock-looks-above-fair-value-on-current-sales","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794306025.481,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (BNTX) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/17/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signal